# Local working-tree backups. This repository is public — it has to be, for
# raw.githubusercontent.com and Pages — so a stray `git add -A` would publish a
# full snapshot. Keep backups out of the index; better still, keep them outside
# the working tree entirely.
Ezekiel-backup-*/

# Perfect Product run logs. These are machine-generated build artifacts, and
# tracking them makes the contract unverifiable: every evidence run dirties the
# tree, and committing the run advances HEAD past the SHA the run recorded, so
# `validate --final` can never see evidence matching the current commit. The
# curated documents beside them — PRODUCT-INTENT, ACCEPTANCE, FINDINGS,
# CHECKPOINT, FINAL-REPORT — stay tracked, and FINAL-REPORT quotes each result
# with the SHA it was produced at.
.perfect-product/evidence/
.perfect-product/EVIDENCE.jsonl
